<title>SPAIN: Telefonica to issue 5-yr dollar convertibles.</title>
<headline>Telefonica to issue 5-yr dollar convertibles.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Telefonica de Espana will issue up to 100 billion pesetas in five-year bonds, denominated in U.S. dollars and convertible into shares, national stock market commission CNMV said on Friday.</p>
<p>CNMV added that bonds will have a nominal value of U.S. $1,000 and are aimed at foreign investors exclusively.</p>
<p>Telefonica's board will set the final total amount of the issue and the date. After that the exact dollar exchange versus the peseta will also be fixed.</p>
</text>
